==Leagues IV: Trailblazer Reloaded==
If you’ve been keeping up with our newsposts, you’ll have seen that the frequent reminders about Leagues Points being calculated on a rolling schedule to protect our web systems. Unfortunately, so many of you are racking up the Points that this system began experiencing errors from re-calculating League Points at such a regular pace! Don’t panic, we’ve fixed the issue – but some players may now find they have a different Point total between Leagues and regular worlds.

If you’re experiencing this issue, please log back into a Leagues World and either open and close the Points interface or complete some new tasks. This should cause the Points to sync correctly again.

In other Leagues news, we’ve fixed an issue where auto-completed Combat Achievements weren’t counting as completed when unlocking the associated region. The following Combat Achievements are affected:

* Faithless Crypt Run (Morytania/Barrows)
* Dress Like You Mean It (Desert/Tempoross)
* Versatile Drainer (Fremennik/Phantom Muspah)
* More Than Just A Ranged Weapon (Fremennik/Phantom Muspah)
* The Worst Ranged Weapon (Asgarnia/Kree’arra)
* Finding The Weak Spot (Wilderness/Corporeal Beast)

Finally, we've fixed an issue with Pyromancer's Garb, so the task can now be completed without any issues.

==Chambers of Xeric==
As promised, we have a selection box of changes for the recently-updated Chambers of Xeric raid.

First up, skeletal mystics will now scale correctly when manually scaling a Raid at creation. Previously, their mystical powers let them see through your ‘invisible mates’ ruse, but we’ve given them a stern talking to about respecting other people’s imaginary friends and now they’ve promised to behave.

We’ve also prevented players from placing Kindling in Storage Units, due to an issue where players could stack a bunch of them to deposit at once for extra Point bonuses. ''Someone’s ''going on the naughty list!

Lastly, we have a pair of smaller bug fixes:

* Tumeken’s Shadow will now splash against the Jewelled Crabs if your Magic Accuracy is -64 or lower.
* Potions now correctly award points when sipped.

You may notice that a couple of the changes we spoke about last week are missing. Firstly, upon further investigation into the Great Grub Bonanza in the Thieving room, we discovered that this behaviour was intended after all. Phew! We also reviewed the implications of removing the attack delay on the Harmonised Nightmare Staff when facing Jewelled Crabs, and discovered that allowing players to cast rapid Fire Strikes would result in those players receiving unusually rapid XP rates. As a result of our investigations, both of these changes have been cancelled.

Nevertheless, we'd like to give a big ol' THANK YOU to everyone who left their feedback! You'll all get extra Cavern Grubs in your stockings this year.

==PvP Rota==
Over the Christmas period, all worlds will be open, regardless of the region. The PvP rota will begin again next year on the 10th January!

The PvP Arena will be using '''Zerker''' loadouts in Ranked Duels and Tournaments this week, starting on Wednesday, with ''''1 Def Pure'''' the following week as this is on an automatic rota.

